  "reason": "1) Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_013: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, ViT-L, weighted fusion → 0.532 acc). With a single data point, we have no basis to judge whether the multimodal combination is actually contributing value or whether the image modality alone achieves similar performance. 2) Question: config_026 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is the exact image-only counterpart to config_013, differing only in the removal of the RNA modality. This cleanly isolates whether adding PCA-encoded RNA to ViT-L features provides a meaningful accuracy/F1 gain. 3) Why best next: Under a limited budget, the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact question is whether multimodal fusion is warranted at all. If config_026 matches or exceeds config_013, the search should pivot toward image-encoder quality or profile/aggregation strategies rather than RNA encoder selection. If config_013 clearly wins, we confirm multimodal is productive and can then spend remaining budget isolating RNA encoder or fusion effects. This single-variable comparison maximizes information per experiment."
}

